summary:
- topic: Athletic Facilities Updates
  text: The board received updates on the South Portland High School Athletic Complex,
    with a projected May 2027 groundbreaking and finalized designs for track areas,
    restrooms, and dark-sky compliant lighting. The South Portland Middle School field
    was also reported ready for internal use this fall after successful grass regrowth
    and safety verification.
- topic: Enrollment and Class Sizes
  text: Overall enrollment shows a slight increase of 20 students compared to last
    year, despite a general trend of declining enrollment in Maine. Kindergarten class
    sizes are being adjusted, with a new teacher being added at Small Elementary,
    necessitating the use of a portable classroom.
- topic: Electronic Device Policy Implementation
  text: The district presented its implementation plan for the new state-mandated
    bell-to-bell ban on personal electronic devices. Approaches vary by grade span,
    with elementary students advised to keep devices at home, middle schoolers locking
    them in lockers, and high schoolers having devices collected and stored in lock
    boxes.
- topic: Student Homelessness Prevention Funding
  text: South Portland received a $40,000 award from the Maine Housing Student Homelessness
    Prevention Program. These funds will provide direct aid to unhoused students and
    families for critical needs like utilities and rent, addressing a significant
    gap in dedicated funding for this vulnerable population.
- topic: Elementary Reconfiguration Progress
  text: The Elementary Reconfiguration Steering Committee shared community feedback,
    highlighting the importance of student diversity and the desire for children to
    remain in the same school for multiple years. A community survey and two public
    forums are scheduled to gather further input on potential scenarios.
- topic: Public Concerns on School Safety and Well-being
  text: Public comments included concerns about the safety and security inequities
    of using portable classrooms at Small Elementary, particularly regarding access
    control and emergency procedures. A middle school student and parent also spoke
    passionately about the need for increased kindness, respect, and mental health
    support for students.
- topic: Financial Transparency and Oversight
  text: Quarterly financial updates will be provided to the City Council to improve
    communication and keep them informed of district finances. These updates will
    first be reviewed by the Finance Committee to ensure alignment and transparency.
